<#
.SYNOPSIS
  CKAM production release script (REFERENCE TEMPLATE, security IF-15 / IF-11 / IF-04, gate GT-F01/F04/F05). Supports -WhatIf.

.DESCRIPTION
  Secret-free, parameterised reference version of the release steps used on the app server since 2026-10-14
  (docs/ai/PRODUCTION_INFRASTRUCTURE.md, "Deploying a new version"). It has NOT been run on the server yet; the
  scripts actually used there live only on the server (EXT-13). Deploying is a separate, explicitly requested step:
  run this only when the owner has asked for a deploy, on the app server, in an elevated Windows PowerShell 5.1.

  Order (each step that changes something is guarded by -WhatIf / -Confirm):
    1. Release folder  <AppRoot>\releases\<Sha>\{backend, frontend-dist}: unpacked from -PackagePath (a .zip built
       on the dev PC) unless it already exists. Completeness is checked. When the package has a RELEASE.json, its
       release id must be <Sha>, and its "alembic_head" becomes the head the database must reach in step 8.
       The release folder is NEVER deleted by this script: the editable install (pip install -e) links the venv
       to releases\<Sha>\backend, and the previous release folder is needed for a switch-back.
    2. Read-only pre-checks of shared\.env WITHOUT printing any value: ENVIRONMENT_NAME is "production";
       JWT_SECRET is at least 32 characters with at least 8 different characters and is not a known placeholder;
       DATABASE_URL is present exactly once, not empty, not in quotes, and not the development default / this
       machine (the app silently falls back to a development database address when it is missing); FRONTEND_DIST_DIR
       is present; the file is not readable by Users / Everyone / Authenticated Users (warning only). Any failed
       rule stops the deploy before anything is touched.
    3. Backup: runs -BackupHook (your script that takes the database backup and exits 0), or requires
       -BackupConfirmed after you ran task CK_Backup_CKASSETMANAGEMENT on the database server and saw "OK" in its
       backup.log. Without one of them the script stops.
    4. Saves shared\.env as shared\.env.pre-<Sha> (never overwrites an earlier copy; a rerun gets a time suffix).
    5. Stops task CKAM-Web and ONLY the python process under shared\venv that listens on the port.
    6. pip install -c <release>\backend\constraints.txt -e <release>\backend into shared\venv (IF-11: the tested
       versions). Needs the Python package index (setuptools for the build, any pin not yet in the venv) or a
       prepared wheel folder: see README.
    7. Sets FRONTEND_DIST_DIR=<release>\frontend-dist (the single release switch), APP_VERSION=<Sha>, and LOG_DIR
       if it is missing. The file is rewritten as UTF-8 without BOM, then the step-2 checks are run again on it.
    8. a) read-only: the code's single Alembic head (= RELEASE.json "alembic_head" when that file exists) and the
          database's revision before the migration ("alembic current").
       b) alembic upgrade head BEFORE the new code starts (new code on the old schema refuses every sign-in), then
          "alembic current" must equal that head.
    9. Starts CKAM-Web, waits for /api/health, then runs verify_release.ps1 (smoke + security test) against it.

  FAILURE HANDLING (roll forward first, docs/security/CKAM_PRODUCTION_ROLLBACK_STRATEGY.md):
    * steps 1-3 fail: nothing was changed; the script stops (exit 2).
    * BRANCH A - a failure in steps 4 to 8a, i.e. BEFORE "alembic upgrade head" was started: the schema is untouched,
      so the script restores shared\.env.pre-<Sha> and restarts the previous release (strategy case 1-A; IF-01
      stays open on the old release, re-plan the deploy at once), exit 1. Exception: when the database is already
      at the new head (an earlier run or a hand migration), the old release cannot run on it, so the script
      stays down as in branch B.
    * BRANCH B - a failure from the moment "alembic upgrade head" is started (the upgrade itself, the head check,
      the start, /api/health, verify_release.ps1): the script does NOT restart the previous release, does NOT run
      alembic downgrade and does NOT restore anything. It leaves CKAM-Web STOPPED, prints a banner with the
      database revision ("alembic current"), writes a STATE line to the deploy log and exits 3. On the new schema
      the previous release cannot record moves / repairs / sales / scrapping (the lifecycle trigger c6e8a0b2d4f6
      refuses them; receives still work, GT-F01) and it re-opens the file-read hole IF-01. The OWNER decides
      between a roll-forward fix (preferred), "alembic downgrade -1" from releases\<Sha>\backend (owner's decision,
      fresh backup first), or restoring the pre-deploy dump (loses everything written since).

  Nothing secret is passed on the command line, printed or logged. alembic output lines that mention a password
  (the one-time first-owner password on an EMPTY database) are hidden in the log; on a brand-new database run
  `alembic upgrade head` by hand instead and keep that line in an admin-only place.

  Exit codes: 0 deployed and verified; 1 branch A (previous release restarted); 2 stopped before anything changed;
  3 branch B (CKAM-Web left stopped, owner decides).

.PARAMETER Sha
  Short git sha of the release (folder name under releases\). Required.
.PARAMETER PackagePath
  Zip with backend\ and frontend-dist\ (and RELEASE.json) at its top level. Not needed when releases\<Sha> exists.
.PARAMETER AppRoot
  Default D:\Citykart_Applications\Citykart_AssetManagement_App
.PARAMETER TaskName
  Scheduled task that runs the launcher. Default CKAM-Web
.PARAMETER Port
  Default 3211
.PARAMETER BackupHook
  Path of a script that takes the pre-deploy database backup and exits 0 when it succeeded.
.PARAMETER BackupConfirmed
  Use instead of -BackupHook when the backup was taken and checked by hand just before.
.PARAMETER SkipPipInstall
  Do not run pip (only when the venv already holds exactly this release's packages).
.PARAMETER HealthTimeoutSeconds
  How long to wait for /api/health after the start. Default 120.

.EXAMPLE
  .\deploy_ckam.ps1 -Sha 1a2b3c4 -PackagePath C:\Windows\Temp\ckam-release-1a2b3c4.zip -BackupConfirmed -WhatIf
.EXAMPLE
  .\deploy_ckam.ps1 -Sha 1a2b3c4 -PackagePath C:\Windows\Temp\ckam-release-1a2b3c4.zip -BackupHook D:\ops\take_ckam_backup.ps1
#>
[CmdletBinding(SupportsShouldProcess = $true, ConfirmImpact = 'Medium')]
param(
    [Parameter(Mandatory = $true)][ValidatePattern('^[0-9a-f]{7,40}$')][string]$Sha,
    [string]$PackagePath = '',
    [string]$AppRoot = 'D:\Citykart_Applications\Citykart_AssetManagement_App',
    [string]$TaskName = 'CKAM-Web',
    [ValidateRange(1, 65535)][int]$Port = 3211,
    [string]$BackupHook = '',
    [switch]$BackupConfirmed,
    [switch]$SkipPipInstall,
    [ValidateRange(10, 900)][int]$HealthTimeoutSeconds = 120
)

$ErrorActionPreference = 'Continue'   # PS 5.1: native stderr (pip/alembic INFO lines) must not abort; exit codes are checked
$stamp = Get-Date -Format 'yyyyMMdd_HHmmss'
$release = Join-Path $AppRoot "releases\$Sha"
$releaseBackend = Join-Path $release 'backend'
$releaseJson = Join-Path $release 'RELEASE.json'
$envFile = Join-Path $AppRoot 'shared\.env'
# Never overwrite the pre-deploy copy of an earlier run (a rerun after a branch-B fix would otherwise lose it).
$envBackup = "$envFile.pre-$Sha"
if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $envBackup) { $envBackup = "$envFile.pre-$Sha.$stamp" }
$python = Join-Path $AppRoot 'shared\venv\Scripts\python.exe'
$logDir = Join-Path $AppRoot 'logs'
$verifyScript = Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'verify_release.ps1'
$strategyDoc = 'docs/security/CKAM_PRODUCTION_ROLLBACK_STRATEGY.md'
$dryRun = [bool]$WhatIfPreference
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $logDir -WhatIf:$false | Out-Null
$logFile = Join-Path $logDir ("deploy_{0}_{1}.log" -f $Sha, $stamp)

# Failure branch state: 'A' until "alembic upgrade head" is started, then 'B' (no automatic switch-back any more).
$script:Phase = 'A'
$script:DbBefore = ''
$script:ExpectedHead = ''
$script:PreviousRelease = ''

function Write-Log([string]$Message) {
    $line = '{0}  {1}' -f (Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss'), $Message
    Write-Host $line
    Add-Content -Path $logFile -Value $line -WhatIf:$false
}
function Stop-Here([string]$Why) { Write-Log "STOPPED: $Why"; Write-Log 'nothing in CKAM was changed (exit 2)'; exit 2 }
function Write-Step([string]$Text) {
    $branch = if ($script:Phase -eq 'A') { 'BRANCH A: restore the previous settings and restart the previous release' }
              else { 'BRANCH B: CKAM-Web stays STOPPED, no switch-back, no downgrade, no restore' }
    Write-Log "$Text   [a failure here -> $branch]"
}

function Read-EnvFile([string]$Path) {
    $map = [ordered]@{}
    foreach ($raw in Get-Content -LiteralPath $Path) {
        if ($raw -match '^\s*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\s*=(.*)$') { $map[$Matches[1]] = $Matches[2] }
    }
    return $map
}
function Set-EnvKey([string[]]$Lines, [string]$Key, [string]$Value) {
    $found = $false
    $out = foreach ($l in $Lines) { if ($l -match "^\s*$Key\s*=") { $found = $true; "$Key=$Value" } else { $l } }
    if (-not $found) { $out = @($out) + "$Key=$Value" }
    return , @($out)
}
function Write-EnvFile([string[]]$Lines) {
    [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($envFile, (($Lines -join "`r`n") + "`r`n"), (New-Object System.Text.UTF8Encoding($false)))
}
function Import-EnvToProcess {
    foreach ($kv in (Read-EnvFile $envFile).GetEnumerator()) { [Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable($kv.Key, $kv.Value, 'Process') }
}

# The app and alembic fall back to a DEVELOPMENT database address when DATABASE_URL is missing (config.py, env.py),
# and the launcher passes values exactly as written. Returns '' when fine, else the reason. The value is never shown.
function Test-DatabaseUrl([string]$Path) {
    $lines = @(Get-Content -LiteralPath $Path | Where-Object { $_ -match '^\s*DATABASE_URL\s*=' })
    if ($lines.Count -eq 0) { return 'DATABASE_URL is missing in shared\.env (the app would silently use the development database address)' }
    if ($lines.Count -gt 1) { return "DATABASE_URL appears $($lines.Count) times in shared\.env (exactly one line is allowed)" }
    $value = ($lines[0] -replace '^\s*DATABASE_URL\s*=', '').Trim()
    $why = ''
    if (-not $value) { $why = 'DATABASE_URL in shared\.env is empty (the app would silently use the development database address)' }
    elseif ($value -match '^["'']') { $why = 'DATABASE_URL in shared\.env is wrapped in quotes (the launcher passes values exactly as written)' }
    elseif ($value -match '^postgresql(\+\w+)?://') {
        $hostPart = ($value -replace '^postgresql(\+\w+)?://', '') -replace '^.*@', ''   # drop scheme and user:password@
        $dbHost = if ($hostPart -match '^\[([^\]]*)\]') { $Matches[1] } else { ($hostPart -split '[/:?]')[0] }
        $hostPart = $null
        if ($value -match 'ckam_dev_pw') { $why = 'DATABASE_URL in shared\.env is the development default' }
        elseif (-not $dbHost) { $why = 'DATABASE_URL in shared\.env names no database host' }
        elseif ($dbHost -in 'localhost', '127.0.0.1', '::1') { $why = "DATABASE_URL in shared\.env points at this machine ($dbHost); the production database is on the database server" }
        else { $script:DbHost = $dbHost }
    } else { $why = 'DATABASE_URL in shared\.env is not a postgresql:// address' }
    $value = $null
    return $why
}

function Invoke-Alembic([string[]]$AlembicArgs) {
    # Runs alembic from the NEW release's backend folder (only it knows the new revisions). Password lines are hidden.
    Push-Location $releaseBackend
    try { $out = & $python -m alembic @AlembicArgs 2>&1 | ForEach-Object { "$_" }; $code = $LASTEXITCODE }
    finally { Pop-Location }
    $shown = foreach ($l in @($out)) { if ($l -match '(?i)password') { '(a line mentioning a password was hidden)' } else { $l } }
    $revs = @(@($out) | Where-Object { $_ -match '^[0-9a-f]{12}\b' } | ForEach-Object { ($_ -split ' ')[0] })
    [pscustomobject]@{ Code = $code; Lines = @($shown); Revs = $revs }
}
function Get-DbRevision {
    # Read-only "alembic current" for the failure banners. Never throws.
    try {
        if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $python) -or -not (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $releaseBackend 'alembic.ini'))) { return 'could not be read (no venv python or no release backend)' }
        Import-EnvToProcess
        if (-not $env:DATABASE_URL) { return 'could not be read (DATABASE_URL is not set)' }
        $r = Invoke-Alembic @('current')
        if ($r.Code -ne 0) { return "could not be read (alembic current exit $($r.Code))" }
        if ($r.Revs.Count -eq 0) { return '(empty: no revision recorded)' }
        return ($r.Revs -join ',')
    } catch { return "could not be read ($($_.Exception.Message))" }
}

function Stop-Ckam {
    if (-not $PSCmdlet.ShouldProcess($TaskName, 'stop CKAM (task + its own python listener only)')) { return }
    Stop-ScheduledTask -TaskName $TaskName -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
    Start-Sleep -Seconds 3
    foreach ($c in @(Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort $Port -State Listen -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue)) {
        $p = Get-CimInstance Win32_Process -Filter "ProcessId = $($c.OwningProcess)"
        if ($p -and $p.ExecutablePath -like (Join-Path $AppRoot 'shared\venv\*')) { Write-Log "stopping CKAM process $($p.ProcessId)"; Stop-Process -Id $p.ProcessId -Force }
        else { Write-Log "WARNING: another program listens on $Port (pid $($c.OwningProcess)); not touching it" }
    }
    Start-Sleep -Seconds 2
    $left = @(Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort $Port -State Listen -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue)
    if ($left.Count -eq 0) { Write-Log "CKAM-Web stopped: nothing listens on port $Port" }
    else { Write-Log "WARNING: something still listens on port $Port (pid $(($left | ForEach-Object { $_.OwningProcess } | Sort-Object -Unique) -join ', ')): check it by hand (runbook step F1)" }
}
function Start-Ckam {
    if ($PSCmdlet.ShouldProcess($TaskName, 'start CKAM')) { Start-ScheduledTask -TaskName $TaskName; Start-Sleep -Seconds 8 }
}
function Wait-Health([int]$Seconds) {
    $deadline = (Get-Date).AddSeconds($Seconds)
    while ((Get-Date) -lt $deadline) {
        try { if ((Invoke-WebRequest -UseBasicParsing -Uri "http://127.0.0.1:$Port/api/health" -TimeoutSec 5).StatusCode -eq 200) { return $true } } catch { }
        Start-Sleep -Seconds 3
    }
    return $false
}

# BRANCH B: from the moment "alembic upgrade head" was started. Never restarts the old release, never downgrades,
# never restores. CKAM stays down (IF-01 cannot be used while nothing listens) until the owner decides.
function Invoke-StayDown([string]$Why) {
    Write-Log "FAILED (branch B, after the migration step started): $Why"
    Stop-Ckam
    $now = Get-DbRevision
    $prev = if ($script:PreviousRelease) { Split-Path -Leaf $script:PreviousRelease } else { '(unknown)' }
    $head = if ($script:ExpectedHead) { $script:ExpectedHead } else { '(unknown)' }
    $before = if ($script:DbBefore) { $script:DbBefore } else { '(not read)' }
    $bar = '=' * 110
    Write-Log $bar
    Write-Log "CKAM DEPLOY $Sha FAILED AFTER THE DATABASE MIGRATION STEP STARTED - CKAM-Web IS LEFT STOPPED"
    Write-Log "Reason: $Why"
    Write-Log "Database now (alembic current): $now   | before this deploy: $before | this release's head: $head"
    Write-Log 'Nothing was switched back, downgraded or restored by this script.'
    Write-Log "shared\.env still selects $Sha (the copy taken before the switch: $envBackup)."
    if ($script:DbBefore -and $now -eq $script:DbBefore -and $now -ne $head) {
        Write-Log 'The database revision is unchanged (all pending migrations run in ONE transaction, a failure rolls back all of them, GT-F04).'
        Write-Log "This is strategy case 1. Do NOT start $Sha on the old schema (every sign-in would fail). The OWNER chooses:"
        Write-Log "  1-A switch back: rollback_release.ps1 -ToSha $prev -ReinstallBackend (IF-01 stays open on it; re-plan at once), or"
        Write-Log '  1-B stay down until the cause is fixed and the deploy is repeated.'
        Write-Log '  No alembic downgrade and no restore: there is nothing to undo.'
    } else {
        Write-Log "The previous release $prev is INCOMPATIBLE with this schema: it cannot record moves, repairs, losses, disposals, sales"
        Write-Log 'or scrapping (lifecycle trigger c6e8a0b2d4f6 refuses them; receives still work), and it RE-OPENS the file-read hole IF-01.'
        Write-Log "Do NOT start $prev. Do NOT run rollback_release.ps1 without the owner's recorded decision."
        Write-Log 'The OWNER decides between: (1) roll forward - fix the cause and start this release again (preferred);'
        Write-Log "  (2) 'alembic downgrade -1' run from releases\$Sha\backend (only the lifecycle guard; fresh backup first);"
        Write-Log '  (3) restore the pre-deploy dump (loses everything written since the backup).'
    }
    Write-Log "See $strategyDoc (cases 2-4 and section 5) and the err/launcher logs in $logDir."
    Write-Log "Keep releases\$Sha (the venv's editable install links to its backend) and releases\$prev. Delete no release folder."
    Write-Log "The task keeps its at-startup trigger: after a server restart it would start $Sha again. Disable-ScheduledTask only on the owner's decision."
    Write-Log $bar
    Write-Log ("STATE: branch=B; ckam_web=stopped; release_selected={0}; previous_release={1}; db_before={2}; db_now={3}; code_head={4}; switched_back=no; downgraded=no; restored=no; exit=3" -f $Sha, $prev, $before, $now, $head)
    exit 3
}

# BRANCH A: before "alembic upgrade head" was started. The schema is untouched, so the previous state may come back.
function Invoke-EarlyRestore([string]$Why) {
    Write-Log "FAILED (branch A, before the migration step started): $Why"
    $prevSha = if ($script:PreviousRelease) { Split-Path -Leaf $script:PreviousRelease } else { '' }
    if ($prevSha -and $prevSha -ne $Sha) {
        # Safety net: if the database is ALREADY at the new head (an earlier run or a hand migration), the previous
        # release cannot run on it - stay down instead.
        $rev = Get-DbRevision
        if ($script:ExpectedHead -and $rev -eq $script:ExpectedHead) {
            $script:DbBefore = $rev
            Invoke-StayDown "$Why (and the database is already at the new head $rev, so the previous release $prevSha must not be restarted)"
        }
        Write-Log "database revision (read-only check): $rev"
    }
    Stop-Ckam
    if ((Test-Path -LiteralPath $envBackup) -and $PSCmdlet.ShouldProcess($envFile, "restore from $envBackup")) {
        Copy-Item -LiteralPath $envBackup -Destination $envFile -Force
        Write-Log "restored shared\.env from $envBackup (the previous release $prevSha is selected again)"
    }
    Start-Ckam
    if (Wait-Health 90) {
        Write-Log "the previous release $prevSha answers again (strategy case 1-A). The schema was not changed by this run."
        Write-Log 'IF-01 is still open on the previous release: re-plan the deploy at once. If pip ran, the venv now holds this release''s pinned packages: smoke-test sign-in and one read.'
    } else {
        Write-Log "THE PREVIOUS RELEASE DID NOT ANSWER - manual action needed (see rollback_release.ps1.template and $strategyDoc case 1)"
    }
    Write-Log "Keep releases\$Sha and releases\$prevSha (delete no release folder)."
    Write-Log ("STATE: branch=A; release_selected={0}; db_changed_by_this_run=no; exit=1" -f $prevSha)
    exit 1
}
function Invoke-Failure([string]$Why) { if ($script:Phase -eq 'B') { Invoke-StayDown $Why } else { Invoke-EarlyRestore $Why } }

Write-Log "=== CKAM deploy $Sha $(if ($dryRun) { '(WhatIf: nothing is changed)' }) ==="

# 1. release folder (kept for good: never deleted by this script)
if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $release 'backend\app\main.py'))) {
    if (-not $PackagePath) { Stop-Here "release folder $release does not exist and no -PackagePath was given" }
    if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $PackagePath)) { Stop-Here "package not found: $PackagePath" }
    if ($PSCmdlet.ShouldProcess($release, "unpack $PackagePath")) {
        New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $release | Out-Null
        Expand-Archive -LiteralPath $PackagePath -DestinationPath $release -Force
    }
} else {
    Write-Log "release folder already there, used as it is (not replaced, not deleted): $release"
}
if (-not $dryRun -or (Test-Path -LiteralPath $release)) {
    foreach ($f in 'backend\app\main.py', 'backend\alembic.ini', 'backend\pyproject.toml', 'backend\constraints.txt', 'frontend-dist\index.html') {
        if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $release $f))) { Stop-Here "release incomplete, missing $f" }
    }
    Write-Log "release folder complete: $release (keep it: the editable install links the venv to its backend)"
    if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $releaseJson) {
        try { $meta = Get-Content -LiteralPath $releaseJson -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json } catch { Stop-Here "RELEASE.json cannot be read: $($_.Exception.Message)" }
        $metaSha = [string]$meta.release_sha_short
        if ($metaSha -and $metaSha -ne $Sha -and -not ([string]$meta.release_sha).StartsWith($Sha)) { Stop-Here "RELEASE.json says release $metaSha, not $Sha" }
        $script:ExpectedHead = [string]$meta.alembic_head
        if ($script:ExpectedHead -and $script:ExpectedHead -notmatch '^[0-9a-f]{12}$') { Stop-Here "RELEASE.json alembic_head '$($script:ExpectedHead)' is not a revision id" }
        Write-Log "RELEASE.json: release $metaSha, the database must reach Alembic head $($script:ExpectedHead)"
    } else {
        Write-Log 'no RELEASE.json in the release folder: the head check uses "alembic heads" of the code only'
    }
} else {
    Write-Log "WhatIf: the package is not unpacked yet; RELEASE.json (release id, alembic_head) would be read from $releaseJson"
}

# 2. pre-checks (read-only; values are never printed)
if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $envFile)) { Stop-Here "settings file not found: $envFile" }
if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $python)) { Stop-Here "venv python not found: $python" }
$settings = Read-EnvFile $envFile
$envName = ([string]$settings['ENVIRONMENT_NAME']).Trim().ToLowerInvariant()
if ($envName -ne 'production') { Stop-Here 'ENVIRONMENT_NAME in shared\.env is not "production"' }
$secret = [string]$settings['JWT_SECRET']
$placeholders = 'change_me', 'change_me_too', 'dev_secret_change_me', 'changeme', 'secret'
$problems = @()
if ($secret.Length -lt 32) { $problems += 'shorter than 32 characters' }
if ((New-Object 'System.Collections.Generic.HashSet[char]' (, $secret.ToCharArray())).Count -lt 8) { $problems += 'fewer than 8 different characters' }
if ($placeholders -contains $secret.Trim().ToLowerInvariant()) { $problems += 'a known placeholder' }
$secret = $null
if ($problems.Count -gt 0) { Stop-Here ('JWT_SECRET fails the production rules: ' + ($problems -join '; ') + ' (the app would refuse to start)') }
Write-Log 'JWT_SECRET meets the production rules (value not shown)'
$script:DbHost = ''
$dbProblem = Test-DatabaseUrl $envFile
if ($dbProblem) { Stop-Here $dbProblem }
Write-Log "DATABASE_URL present exactly once (value not shown; database host: $($script:DbHost))"
if (-not ([string]$settings['FRONTEND_DIST_DIR']).Trim()) { Stop-Here 'FRONTEND_DIST_DIR is missing in shared\.env' }
if ($settings['TRUSTED_PROXIES']) { Write-Log 'WARNING: TRUSTED_PROXIES is set; CKAM runs without a proxy here, it should be empty (N2/N3)' }
$wide = @((Get-Acl -LiteralPath $envFile).Access | Where-Object { $_.IdentityReference -match '\\(Users|Everyone|Authenticated Users)$|^Everyone$' })
if ($wide.Count -gt 0) { Write-Log ('WARNING: shared\.env is readable by ' + (($wide | ForEach-Object { $_.IdentityReference }) -join ', ') + ' - restrict it to Administrators, SYSTEM and the task account') }
$previousDist = [string]$settings['FRONTEND_DIST_DIR']
$script:PreviousRelease = Split-Path -Parent $previousDist
if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $script:PreviousRelease 'backend\app\main.py'))) {
    Write-Log "WARNING: the current release folder $($script:PreviousRelease) is incomplete or missing: a branch-A switch-back could not start it"
}
Write-Log "pre-checks passed; current release: $($script:PreviousRelease)"

# 3. backup
if ($BackupHook) {
    if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $BackupHook)) { Stop-Here "backup hook not found: $BackupHook" }
    if ($PSCmdlet.ShouldProcess($BackupHook, 'run the pre-deploy database backup')) {
        & powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File $BackupHook
        if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { Stop-Here "backup hook failed with exit code $LASTEXITCODE - nothing was changed" }
        Write-Log 'backup hook finished OK'
    }
} elseif ($BackupConfirmed) {
    Write-Log 'backup confirmed by the operator (-BackupConfirmed)'
} else {
    Stop-Here 'take the database backup first (task CK_Backup_CKASSETMANAGEMENT on the database server, check backup.log says OK), then rerun with -BackupConfirmed, or pass -BackupHook'
}

# 4. keep the current settings for a branch-A switch-back
Write-Step "step 4: save shared\.env as $envBackup"
if ($PSCmdlet.ShouldProcess($envFile, "copy to $envBackup")) { Copy-Item -LiteralPath $envFile -Destination $envBackup -Force; Write-Log "saved $envBackup" }

# 5. stop
Write-Step "step 5: stop $TaskName"
Stop-Ckam

# 6. packages (IF-11: exactly the tested versions; needs the package index or a wheel folder, see README)
Write-Step 'step 6: pip install -c constraints.txt -e <release>\backend'
if ($SkipPipInstall) { Write-Log 'pip install skipped (-SkipPipInstall)' }
elseif ($PSCmdlet.ShouldProcess($releaseBackend, 'pip install -c constraints.txt -e')) {
    $pip = & $python -m pip install --disable-pip-version-check -c (Join-Path $releaseBackend 'constraints.txt') -e $releaseBackend 2>&1 | ForEach-Object { "$_" }
    $code = $LASTEXITCODE
    $pip | Select-Object -Last 5 | ForEach-Object { Write-Log "pip: $_" }
    if ($code -ne 0) { Invoke-Failure "pip install failed with exit code $code" }
}

# 7. switch the release (one setting) + release id, then the step-2 checks again on the written file
Write-Step "step 7: set FRONTEND_DIST_DIR=$release\frontend-dist, APP_VERSION=$Sha"
if ($PSCmdlet.ShouldProcess($envFile, "set FRONTEND_DIST_DIR=$release\frontend-dist, APP_VERSION=$Sha")) {
    $lines = Get-Content -LiteralPath $envFile
    $lines = Set-EnvKey $lines 'FRONTEND_DIST_DIR' (Join-Path $release 'frontend-dist')
    $lines = Set-EnvKey $lines 'APP_VERSION' $Sha
    if (-not $settings['LOG_DIR']) { $lines = Set-EnvKey $lines 'LOG_DIR' (Join-Path $AppRoot 'logs\app') }
    Write-EnvFile $lines
    Write-Log 'settings switched to the new release (FRONTEND_DIST_DIR, APP_VERSION)'
    $again = Read-EnvFile $envFile
    if (([string]$again['ENVIRONMENT_NAME']).Trim().ToLowerInvariant() -ne 'production') { Invoke-Failure 'after the switch ENVIRONMENT_NAME is no longer "production"' }
    $dbProblem = Test-DatabaseUrl $envFile
    if ($dbProblem) { Invoke-Failure "after the switch: $dbProblem" }
    if ([string]$again['FRONTEND_DIST_DIR'] -ne (Join-Path $release 'frontend-dist')) { Invoke-Failure 'after the switch FRONTEND_DIST_DIR does not select the new release' }
    Write-Log 'switched settings re-checked: ENVIRONMENT_NAME, DATABASE_URL (value not shown), FRONTEND_DIST_DIR'
}

# 8a. read-only: the code's head and the database revision BEFORE the migration (still branch A)
Write-Step 'step 8a: alembic heads (code) and alembic current (database), read-only'
if ($PSCmdlet.ShouldProcess($releaseBackend, 'alembic heads + alembic current (read-only)')) {
    Import-EnvToProcess
    if (-not $env:DATABASE_URL) { Invoke-Failure 'DATABASE_URL is not set in the process - alembic would use the development fallback' }
    $h = Invoke-Alembic @('heads')
    if ($h.Code -ne 0 -or $h.Revs.Count -ne 1) { Invoke-Failure "alembic heads did not give exactly one head (exit $($h.Code), heads '$($h.Revs -join ',')')" }
    $codeHead = $h.Revs[0]
    if ($script:ExpectedHead -and $codeHead -ne $script:ExpectedHead) { Invoke-Failure "the code's head $codeHead is not RELEASE.json's alembic_head $($script:ExpectedHead)" }
    $script:ExpectedHead = $codeHead
    $c = Invoke-Alembic @('current')
    if ($c.Code -ne 0) { $c.Lines | Select-Object -Last 3 | ForEach-Object { Write-Log "alembic: $_" }; Invoke-Failure "alembic current failed with exit code $($c.Code) (database not reachable?)" }
    $script:DbBefore = ($c.Revs -join ',')
    Write-Log "database before the migration: '$($script:DbBefore)'; code head: $codeHead"
    if ($script:DbBefore -eq $codeHead) { Write-Log 'the database is already at this head: the upgrade will be a no-op' }
} elseif (-not $dryRun) {
    Invoke-Failure 'the read-only alembic check was declined at the -Confirm prompt'
} else {
    Write-Log "WhatIf: would read alembic heads (must be ONE head$(if ($script:ExpectedHead) { " = RELEASE.json $($script:ExpectedHead)" })) and alembic current from $releaseBackend"
}

# 8b. migrations BEFORE the start. From the moment the upgrade starts there is NO automatic switch-back (branch B).
Write-Log 'step 8b: alembic upgrade head   [from the moment it starts, a failure -> BRANCH B: CKAM-Web stays STOPPED, no switch-back, no downgrade, no restore]'
if ($PSCmdlet.ShouldProcess($releaseBackend, 'alembic upgrade head')) {
    $script:Phase = 'B'
    Write-Log 'migration step started: from now on a failure leaves CKAM-Web stopped (branch B)'
    $up = Invoke-Alembic @('upgrade', 'head')
    foreach ($l in $up.Lines) { Write-Log "alembic: $l" }
    if ($up.Code -ne 0) { Invoke-Failure "alembic upgrade failed with exit code $($up.Code)" }
    $c = Invoke-Alembic @('current')
    $current = ($c.Revs -join ',')
    if ($c.Code -ne 0 -or $current -ne $script:ExpectedHead) { Invoke-Failure "after the upgrade the database is at '$current' but the release's head is '$($script:ExpectedHead)'" }
    Write-Log "database at head $current"
} elseif ($dryRun) {
    $script:Phase = 'B'
    Write-Log "WhatIf: would run alembic upgrade head, then require alembic current = $(if ($script:ExpectedHead) { $script:ExpectedHead } else { 'the code''s head' })"
} else {
    # Declined at a -Confirm prompt: the schema is untouched, never start the new code on the old schema.
    Invoke-Failure 'the migration step was declined at the -Confirm prompt'
}

# 9. start + smoke test (still branch B)
Write-Step "step 9: start $TaskName, wait for /api/health, run verify_release.ps1"
Start-Ckam
if ($dryRun) {
    $prev = Split-Path -Leaf $script:PreviousRelease
    Write-Log "WhatIf: would wait for http://127.0.0.1:$Port/api/health and run $verifyScript -BaseUrl http://127.0.0.1:$Port -ExpectedRelease $Sha -ReleaseDir $release -LauncherLogDir $logDir -LocalProcessCheck Require"
    Write-Log 'WhatIf: failure handling plan (nothing failed in this dry run):'
    Write-Log '  steps 1-3 (release folder, pre-checks, backup)           -> STOP, nothing changed, exit 2'
    Write-Log "  steps 4-8a (save settings, stop, pip, switch, read heads) -> BRANCH A: restore $envBackup, restart the previous release $prev (schema untouched), exit 1"
    Write-Log "  steps 8b-9 (alembic upgrade head, head check, start, health, verify) -> BRANCH B: $TaskName left STOPPED, $prev NOT restarted, no downgrade, no restore, banner + STATE line, exit 3"
    Write-Log "  release folders releases\$Sha and releases\$prev are kept in every case"
    Write-Log '=== WhatIf finished: nothing in CKAM was changed (only this log file was written) ==='
    exit 0
}
if (-not (Wait-Health $HealthTimeoutSeconds)) { Invoke-Failure 'the new release did not answer /api/health' }
Write-Log 'health ok'
& powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File $verifyScript -BaseUrl "http://127.0.0.1:$Port" -ExpectedRelease $Sha -ReleaseDir $release -LauncherLogDir $logDir -LocalProcessCheck Require -OutCsv (Join-Path $logDir "verify_$Sha.csv") | ForEach-Object { Write-Log "verify: $_" }
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { Invoke-Failure "verify_release.ps1 reported a failure (exit $LASTEXITCODE), see verify_$Sha.csv" }
Write-Log "=== deploy $Sha finished OK. Keep releases\$Sha (the venv's editable install links to it) and the previous release folder ($($script:PreviousRelease)). ==="
Write-Log ("STATE: branch=none; ckam_web=running; release_selected={0}; db_now={1}; exit=0" -f $Sha, $script:ExpectedHead)
exit 0
